  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access — Trusted Relationship", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "At 2027-09-14 10:02:11 CEST, the B2B API gateway 10.108.57.184 received a GET /api/v1/partners/acmecorp-001/orders carrying header X-API-Token: partner_token_abc123, X-Partner-ID: acmecorp-001, User-Agent 'AcmeCorp-Integration/3.4', from data.srcip=91.108.4.228. The token is a valid contracted partner credential — its agreed scope is the partner's own orders endpoint. The request itself is in-scope and would normally be benign; what is anomalous is the SOURCE: 91.108.4.228 is a Telegram-datacenter / suspicious-hosting IP (ASN 62041) that has never appeared in the acmecorp-001 partner's historical API source ranges. This is the token-validation probe that precedes scope abuse.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92901 'Partner API token used outside normal scope' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1199. The univariate signature: a contracted partner token (X-API-Token partner_token_abc123) presented from a data.srcip outside the partner's known ASN baseline. First request is in-scope (orders) so this step alone is low-confidence — it is the anchor that the following out-of-scope steps confirm.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T10:02:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Discovery — out-of-scope endpoint enumeration", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "Between 10:04 and 10:11 CEST, the same token + same data.srcip=91.108.4.228 walked three endpoints OUTSIDE the acmecorp-001 contracted scope: GET /api/v1/partners/acmecorp-001/clients (partner client-list enumeration), GET /api/v1/admin/users (admin user directory — explicitly NOT in any partner contract), GET /api/v1/export/customer-data (bulk customer-data export). Each request reused header X-API-Token: partner_token_abc123 and User-Agent 'AcmeCorp-Integration/3.4'. The sequential, ~20-second-spaced walk from a contracted endpoint into /admin and /export paths is the scope-escalation signature.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31501 'Sensitive endpoint access via partner credential' fired for data.url matching /api/v1/admin/users and /api/v1/export/customer-data with the partner token present. Same data.srcip and same X-API-Token as step 1 ties it to the same session. rule.mitre.id=T1199.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T10:04:30+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Privilege Escalation — admin control-surface write", "technique": "T1199", "what_happened": "At 10:14:39 CEST the same token + data.srcip=91.108.4.228 issued POST /api/v1/admin/settings with JSON body {\"mfa_enforcement\":false,\"session_timeout\":86400} — an attempt to disable MFA enforcement tenant-wide and extend session lifetime to 24h. This is a state-changing write to the admin control surface using a partner credential that has zero contractual authority over tenant security settings. It is the objective the prior steps were leading toward.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92901 re-fired at higher level for an HTTP POST (write) to data.url=/api/v1/admin/settings carrying X-API-Token partner_token_abc123 from data.srcip=91.108.4.228. The POST method + admin/settings path + security-weakening body is the most severe event of the chain.", "first_seen": "2027-09-14T10:14:39+0200"}
